This one is mostly about the boundary rules, so I'll go through them before writing code. Paragraphs split on lines that are blank or whitespace-only; I'll treat any run of such lines as one separator. Within a paragraph, I fill greedily: a word joins the current line if `len(cur) + 1 + len(word) <= width`, otherwise the line is flushed. A word longer than `width` is flushed as its own pieces of exactly `width` characters, and the last piece becomes the current line so the next word can still join it when it fits. Between paragraphs I emit a single `""`, and I only emit separators between non-empty paragraphs, so leading or trailing blank lines produce nothing.

